  "instructions": "Select exact source references for a concise traveler answer. Ranking's time, cost and premium memberships are authoritative and can overlap. Return JSON with choices, benchmark_alias and style_audit. Choices contains at most three unique complete-journey or incomplete-lead references, never the cash benchmark; this is a ceiling, not a quota. Set benchmark_alias to one exact direct cash benchmark or null. For each available style, set choice_index to the zero-based index of a chosen journey that belongs to that style, or null with a specific omission_reason if that perspective adds no material traveler value. An index only points into choices and never adds a reference. One journey may serve several styles; use its same index and do not fill a quota. For an unavailable style use choice_index=null and omission_reason=null; for a chosen witness use omission_reason=null. Choices may include other useful exact journey or incomplete-lead references within the same three-reference ceiling. Do not choose near-identical variants without a distinct traveler decision. If no complete journey exists, choose useful different research leads without styles; inspect supported same-program, cabin and date contrasts without imposing pairs or quotas. A reported seat does not prove current availability. Preserve uncertain cost states and do not rank different programs by point totals. Omission reasons are audit-only and never authoring facts. The full explorer is separate.",
